From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Melanie Riise <me@mriise.net>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:44:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [zlib][x86] Enable AVX-512 CRC-32 in the GN build

The AVX-512 VPCLMULQDQ kernel (https://crrev.com/c/4374529) is only
built by CMake. With the parent CLs it is selected at runtime only when
the CPU and OS support it, and is compiled through its target attribute.

AMD Ryzen 9 7950X: CRC-32 alone runs at 74 GiB/s vs 37 GiB/s for AVX2
at 64 KiB. zlib_bench gzip decompression gains +2.9% geomean over AVX2,
within noise (the zlib wrapper, which has no CRC-32, moved +2.1%), and
+7.7% over SSE4.2. Intel CPUs, where 512-bit instructions may lower
clocks, have not been measured.

Bug: TODO_FILE_CRBUG
---
 third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn b/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn
index 65074c0b..99a5e6f0 100644
--- a/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/zlib/BUILD.gn
@@ -229,6 +229,7 @@ config("zlib_crc32_simd_config") {
     defines = [
       "CRC32_SIMD_SSE42_PCLMUL",
       "CRC32_SIMD_AVX2_PCLMUL",
+      "CRC32_SIMD_AVX512_PCLMUL",
     ]
   }
 }
